    <string name="settings_scoped_note">Showing what applies here — the full settings live on the home screen.</string>
    <string name="settings_character_speed">Character speed</string>
    <string name="settings_qrq_note">\n\nQRQ territory — %1$s WPM. Great for pushing instant recognition once 30+ feels comfortable.</string>
    <string name="settings_speed_footer">Character speed is how fast the dits and dahs are sent. Farnsworth keeps each character at full speed but adds extra space between characters, down to the effective speed, so you have time to recognise each one. Applies to words, groups and other multi-character content — single characters are unaffected.</string>
    <string name="settings_speed_warning">Below %1$s WPM it\'s easy to start counting the dits and dahs instead of hearing each character as a single sound. Training at %2$s+ WPM builds instant, by-ear recognition, which is the whole point of the Koch method. If you need more time to answer, raise \"Recognition target\" or lower the Farnsworth speed instead of slowing the code.</string>
